# yaourt — real-world examples

AUR helper for Arch Linux. Note: yaourt is unmaintained — on a current
Arch box use `paru` or `yay`, which take the same pacman-style flags.
(Not applicable on openSUSE — that's `zypper` / OBS territory.)

## pacman parity

```sh
# All pacman commands work the same way with yaourt —
# see the pacman cheatsheet. To install a package:
pacman -S <package name>
yaourt -S <package name>

# The difference: yaourt also queries the Arch User Repository (AUR)
# and builds requested packages from source when needed.
```

## What yaourt adds over pacman

```sh
# Search for a package interactively and install it
yaourt <package name>

# Update package db and upgrade everything out of date,
# including AUR and development packages (git, svn, hg...)
yaourt -Suya --devel

# Skip constant confirmation prompts
yaourt -Suya --noconfirm

# Build a package from source
yaourt -Sb <package name>
```

## Modern equivalents (paru/yay)

```sh
# Same ideas, maintained tools
yay -S <package name>
yay -Sua            # upgrade AUR packages
paru -Sua --devel   # include -git style dev packages
```

## Flag reference

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-S PKG` | install (repo or AUR) |
| `-Ss TERM` | search repos + AUR |
| `-Suya` | full system + AUR upgrade |
| `--devel` | also rebuild VCS (-git/-svn) packages |
| `-Sb PKG` | build from source |
| `--noconfirm` | skip confirmation prompts |
